    "Mouth breathing is the classic example. A child who breathes through their mouth often sleeps poorly; poor sleep looks like ADHD in the classroom; shallow breathing dulls appetite and drives picky eating; and the cycle compounds. This airway-sensory connection is the heart of Dr. Marielly's Therastacking approach, and it's why families are referred to us by dentists, orthodontists, and ENTs across Los Angeles.",
